          "author": "Momma Bear Audio",
          "description": "Interactive scenarios where kids practice persuasion and compromise.Think your kid has what it takes to make the deal? The Negotiator is an interactive audio challenge that puts kids right in the middle of tricky, real-life situations where they’ll need to think, communicate, compromise, and get creative!Across a series of short scenarios, kids will negotiate over the last cookie, battle for the best seat, work through disagreements with friends, make chore swaps, stretch a limited budget, and tackle increasingly difficult challenges. Each round gives listeners time to come up with their own solution before exploring different ways the problem could be solved.Along the way, they’ll build their very own Negotiator Toolkit, learning practical skills like making a counteroffer, asking good questions, understanding what someone else really wants, identifying their own priorities, creating win-win solutions, and knowing when a deal just isn’t worth it.There isn’t always one right answer, and that’s the fun of it!Listen. Think. Get creative. And make the deal!Run time: 28 min\n\nLooking for other free audio sources, ideas and inspo? Maybe you want to submit a request for some sort of specific audio for your kids? Join my FB Group! I am always taking suggestions and working to get the audio your kids want.\nToyo Momma Bear source: ba4135eed989ba1951d86b9958d518fe1c1aa22d5a2c709a24e787939d5edb02",
